WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.040
Adolescent Sheldon Cooper isn't as&nbsp;
young as he once was. Come Season 7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.820
it might be time for Young Sheldon's&nbsp;
showrunners to hang up the towel.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:14.760
As a spinoff from one of the most widely memed&nbsp;
sitcoms of the 21st century, snide comments about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:20.100
the existence of Young Sheldon have gotten older&nbsp;
than the series star itself at this point. They're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.380
also fairly unwarranted, as the is consistently&nbsp;
one of the highest-rated network hits on TV.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.200
However, the very title of Young Sheldon implies&nbsp;
the series can't expand as endlessly as its parent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.540
program, The Big Bang Theory, and in fact — when&nbsp;
we look at the larger narrative — we're rapidly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:41.700
approaching the point where he will finally age&nbsp;
up, and not be considered young anymore. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.320
this reason, we believe the seventh season of the&nbsp;
series should mark the end of the sitcom's run.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.880
As regular viewers of the spinoff series&nbsp;
will recall, adult Sheldon confirmed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.740
father's premature death through voice over at&nbsp;
the end of Season 4, and it seems that the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.080
show's trajectory is starting to evolve more&nbsp;
toward that inevitable life event. While the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.400
events were long passed in the time The Big&nbsp;
Bang Theory takes place, this loss is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.200
to hit a lot harder now that viewers have spent 6&nbsp;
seasons getting to know Sheldon's father, George.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.120
In fact, George is such a major character&nbsp;
in the series it's quite possible his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.140
death will be so devastating that the&nbsp;
showrunners may need to call it quits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.980
just to preserve the show's legacy. We've&nbsp;
already caught a glimpse of the emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.520
wait his character's health carries&nbsp;
after his heart attack in season 1.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:31.380
Geoge's physical well-being isn't the only&nbsp;
aspect of his character the show is zeroing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.600
in on. Throughout season 5, George also begins&nbsp;
developing an interesting relationship with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.081
recently divorced neighbor, Brenda while conflict&nbsp;
with his own wife brews under the surface.

00:01:42.081 --> 00:01:43.701
"Who knew you were so handy?"

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:46.161
"Yeah, there's just things&nbsp;
guys need to be good at."

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:47.530
"What else you good at?"

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:52.740
The simmering pot begins to bubble when Mary gets&nbsp;
a new job at the local bar with Brenda, and she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.480
learns that Brenda has a secret love interest.&nbsp;
The tension built further when, in Season 6,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:03.300
Sheldon's sister reveals that Brenda's son caught&nbsp;
George and her alone together. With so much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.160
foreshadowing toward this plotpoint, an official&nbsp;
confirmation of the affair seems inevitable.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:13.020
With all this tension built, and various&nbsp;
other members of the family also experiencing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.880
milestones throughout its run, Season 6&nbsp;
has taken many of the narrative turns of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.320
a typical sitcom's penultimate season,&nbsp;
which only solidifies the fact that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.440
would make perfect sense to round&nbsp;
things out with one final season.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.380
Another important factor to consider about the&nbsp;
significance of George's passing and infidelity is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:36.360
the effect it will inevitably have on Sheldon.&nbsp;
It's possible that losing his father, or the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.400
inevitable drama that will ensue in the Cooper&nbsp;
household when George's affair gets out, may turn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.480
out to be the catalyst for adult Sheldon's&nbsp;
difficulties with emotional intelligence.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.700
Childhood traumas like these would well-inform&nbsp;
Sheldon's lack of trust and intimacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.800
which he slowly overcomes with Amy throughout&nbsp;
The Big Bang Theory. It also indicates the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:59.880
of a fairly complacent era for the&nbsp;
famously complicated Cooper family.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.900
What's more, we already have some&nbsp;
insight into how Sheldon reacts to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:07.200
these events. In the Season 11&nbsp;
episode of The Big Bang Theory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.820
"The Sibling Realignment," an adult Georgie&nbsp;
confronts Sheldon for leaving home so soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.500
after their father's death. He rightfully calls&nbsp;
him out for being selfish as their family was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.240
in pieces after George's passing. Georgie had to&nbsp;
step up and take care of his mother and sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.980
on top of his own family, while Sheldon&nbsp;
moved out to California for graduate school.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.640
Once Sheldon leaves home, it will&nbsp;
be almost impossible to consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.120
him a child. These life-changing&nbsp;
events will make him seem older,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.740
while also adding a few thousand miles&nbsp;
between him and his family. After this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:43.020
it's hard to imagine how the show could continue&nbsp;
past Season 7 without defying its basic premise.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:47.760
Season 6 has also been a palate cleanser&nbsp;
from Sheldon's know-it-all antics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.920
which usually hog the center spotlight.&nbsp;
With Georgie's baby mama drama, fans have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.240
even started calling for a spin-off. This is&nbsp;
an intriguing idea to keep the series alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.920
though it will definitely need to veer&nbsp;
away from its "Young Sheldon" title.&nbsp;

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.660
A&nbsp;spin-off of a spin-off isn't an unheard-of&nbsp;
concept, either, even if they are a bit rare.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:11.520
In this form, we could still see Iain Armitage&nbsp;
as the brilliant young grad student through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.740
guest appearances, or even over the phone. This&nbsp;
format has already been tested on the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.820
with Jim Parsons reprising his role&nbsp;
as adult Sheldon via narration.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.900
The timing couldn't be better, either.&nbsp;
With the family mourning the loss of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.600
their patriarch and adjusting&nbsp;
to life without Sheldon around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.500
the main focus could easily shift to&nbsp;
Georgie and Mandy's new little one.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.120
While we certainly don't want to say goodbye to&nbsp;
George's character, the show's been hinting at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:40.560
his fate since the jump, and it's finally&nbsp;
time to throw the dart at the bullseye.

